  "fidelity": {
    "functional": {
      "claims": "Nets, ports, LD2, LD3, B1, B2 and the jumpers as parts; the STM32F446RE runs its firmware (see its description), its HSE an 8 MHz clock on PH0 (HSEBYP needed, as on the real board) and its LSE the X2 crystal. The ST-LINK/V2-1's virtual COM port is the session's console on USART2 (PA2/PA3) and a serial port on the host; Arduino D0/D1 are not connected to PA3/PA2, as SB62/SB63 are off from the factory.",
      "omissions": [
        "the ST-LINK/V2-1 itself: its USB enumeration, the mass-storage drag-and-drop programming, SWD and its NRST drive (the session programs and debugs the board, ADR-031)",
        "the VCP's bytes reach USART2 directly, not as frames on PA2/PA3",
        "LD1 (COM), the ST-LINK's tricolour LED",
        "the solder bridges are fixed in their factory state (SB62/SB63 off, SB56/SB51 on, SB16/SB50 on, SB45/SB57 on)",
        "a single JP5 shunt cannot sit on both positions; the two switches here can",
        "CN7 pin 29 (PH0, SB55 off) and the unpopulated X3, C33, C34, R35 and R37",
        "CN3 (the ST-LINK's SWD) and CN4 (SWD to an external target)"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    },
    "timed": {
      "claims": "As functional.",
      "omissions": [
        "as functional"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    },
    "electrical": {
      "claims": "The power paths of UM1724 6.3: the ST-LINK's USB 5 V (U5V) through T2 (STS7PF30L, enabled by PWR_ENn low) and JP5 pins 1-2 to +5V; VIN (7 to 12 V) through U3 (LD1117S50) and D4 (STPS2L30A) to E5V and, with JP5 on pins 2-3, to +5V; U4 (LD39050PU33R) makes +3.3V and JP6 (IDD) carries it to VDD, VBAT and (through SB57) VDDA. LD3 shows +5V, LD2 is lit by PA5 through 510 ohm, B1 pulls PC13 low through R29 against R30 (4.7 k) with C15 filtering it, C14 holds NRST low for about 1.5 ms at power-on against the STM32's pull-up, C26 sits on VCAP_1, R33 holds BOOT0 low, and X2 is a BVD equivalent.",
      "omissions": [
        "the ST-LINK's current negotiation: PWR_ENn is low as after a host has granted 300 mA (a 100 mA port, JP1, and the host's refusal are not modelled)",
        "the ST-LINK's own supply (U1, LD3985M33R) and current",
        "decoupling and bulk capacitors (C16 to C25, C27 to C30)",
        "C31/C32 and R34/R36 around X2",
        "ESD protection",
